Verse 1:
[C]O listen to our [G/D]wondrous story,
[C]Counted [F]once among [G]the [C]lost;
[C]Yet One came down from [G/D]heaven’s glory,
[C]Saving [F]us at [C/G]awful cost!

Refrain:
[C]Who saved us from [Dm]eternal [Em]loss?
[C]Who but God's Son [G]upon [F]the cross?
[Dm]What did He do? [C]He [G]died for [Em]you!
[C]Where [G7]is [Am]He [Dm/F]now? [G]Believe [C]it thou,
[C]In heaven [G/D]interceding! [C]In heaven [F]interceding!

Verse 2:
[C]No angel could His [G/D]place [Dm]have [G]taken,
[C]Highest [F]of the [C/G]high [G]tho' [C]he;
[C]The loved One on the [G/D]cross [Dm]forsaken
[C]Was One [F]of the [C/G]Godhead three!

Verse 3:
[C]Will you surrender [G/D]to [Dm]this [G]Savior?
[C]To His [F]scepter [C/G]humbly bow?
[C]You, too, shall come to [G/D]know [Dm]His [G]favor,
[C]He will [F]save you, [C/G]save [G]you [C]now.
